<p class="govuk-body">Your order is a community order. It lets you stay in the community to serve your sentence instead of going to prison.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">The court could ask you to:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li>do unpaid work, which is sometimes called community service</li>
  <li>go to appointments</li>
  <li>take part in activities to stop you from offending again</li>
  <li>get treatment or support</li>
</ul>
<p class="govuk-body">It is important to remember if you do not follow the rules of your order you could go back to court.</p>
<p class="govuk-body">The court might decide to:</p>
<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li>give you more strict rules to follow in the community</li>
  <li>add more time to your order</li>
</ul>
